  "## What was repaired

Five `cloud-itonami` appviews rendered *\"No public route is declared next to this
app surface\"* while their `wrangler.jsonc` declared the very address serving the
page, listed no vars against those declared, and carried a `relativePath` pointing
into the monorepo the repository was extracted from.

    app-saiban     routeCount 0 -> 1   vars 0 -> 10
    app-scheduler  routeCount 0 -> 2
    app-warehouse  routeCount 0 -> 2
    app-wvme       routeCount 0 -> 2
    car-sim        routeCount 0 -> 2   routes now [c4r51m00.etzhayyim.com/*, driver.etzhayyim.com/*]

Each landed as a child-repo commit, a server-side merge, and a west pin advance:
`5e0b1b5`, `026d6bc`, `077c04a`, `8b872c0`, `ac3cfb1`.

Measured after: `5 page(s) carry a summary; 5 compared; 0 differ from their
wrangler`. **The `5 compared` is the load-bearing half of that sentence** -- before
ADR-2608197000 the same run printed `0 differ` whether or not anything had been
opened.

## The procedure, because the remaining 91 repositories need it

`--apply` writes into the tree it is pointed at, and that must never be the shared
checkout. Per repository:

    git -C orgs/<org>/<repo> worktree add -b <branch> <scratch>/wt-<repo> <org>/main
    cp -R <scratch>/wt-<repo> /tmp/genroot-<repo>/orgs/<org>/<repo>
    nbb scripts/gen-appview-page-summary.cljs --root /tmp/genroot-<repo> \
        --names <repo> --apply
    # copy back only the +page.svelte files that actually changed, then
    # commit -> push -> gh api .../merges -> nbb scripts/west-pin-put.cljs <repo> <sha>

Two traps, both hit today:

- **The remote is named after the org, not `origin`** in west checkouts, so
  `<org>/main` is the branch to fork from.
- **zsh does not word-split**, so `set -- $pair` inside a loop passes the whole
  string as one argument and `west-pin-put.cljs` prints its usage four times in a
  row. Feed pairs through `while read -r name sha` instead. This is the same trap
  CLAUDE.md records for `west update $NAMES`; it applies to every loop that thinks
  it is splitting a variable.

## Why the detector's own count has not moved yet

The shared checkout is 23 commits behind `origin/main` and cannot fast-forward: a
neighbouring session has `90-docs/kaizen/kaiyu-kaizen.ledger.edn` modified in the
working tree. **That file was left alone.** It is an append-only ledger being
written by a live session, and stashing it to make a number move today is not worth
it -- `west update` will pick the new pins up when the tree syncs, and the fifteen
findings these five repositories account for (of 287) will resolve then.

The verification above does not depend on that: it runs against the five committed
worktrees directly.

## Note on the index.lock

Four times today `git merge` failed on `.git/index.lock`. The first three were
stale (zero bytes, no holder by `lsof`) and clearing them was right. **The fourth
was not**: it reappeared within a second of removal, because the neighbouring
session is committing continuously (`Merge agent/pin-app-dougaka…` and siblings).
Retry, do not clear, when a lock comes back immediately -- removing a live lock
races the process that owns it."}]
